files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68d41a9bbc98893b635126e0_CCS%20Headshots%20(11)-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68d41a9bbc98893b635126e0_CCS%20Headshots%20(11)-p-1600.png 1600w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68d41a9bbc98893b635126e0_CCS%20Headshots%20(11).png 2000w" alt="" class="uui-testimonial15_customer-image"/></div><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-info"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-heading"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/enkitoto/"><strong>Kamil Kluza</strong></a></div><div class="uui-text-size-small">COO, Climate X<br/></div></div></div></div></div><div class="text-block-3"><strong class="bold-text-7">Table 2</strong></div><div class="text-block-2"><strong>Climate Adaptation and Mitigation</strong><br/>What are companies doing to adjust to a world where we won’t meet the climate goals to reduce emissions? <br/></div><div class="text-block-3"></div><div class="w-row"><div class="w-col w-col-6"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-image-wrapper"><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68d41ac8008f93f888730278_CCS%20Headshots%20(12).png" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 479px) 407px, (max-width: 767px) 198px, 180px" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68d41ac8008f93f888730278_CCS%20Headshots%20(12)-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68d41ac8008f93f888730278_CCS%20Headshots%20(12)-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68d41ac8008f93f888730278_CCS%20Headshots%20(12)-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68d41ac8008f93f888730278_CCS%20Headshots%20(12)-p-1600.png 1600w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68d41ac8008f93f888730278_CCS%20Headshots%20(12).png 2000w" alt="" class="uui-testimonial15_customer-image"/></div><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-info"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-heading"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/adriannaalterman/"><strong>Claudine Emeott</strong></a></div><div class="uui-text-size-small">Partner, Salesforce Ventures<br/></div></div></div></div><div class="w-col w-col-6"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-image-wrapper"><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68d41afd0c39a807cfbd0cba_CCS%20Headshots%20(13).png" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 479px) 407px, (max-width: 767px) 198px, 180px" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68d41afd0c39a807cfbd0cba_CCS%20Headshots%20(13)-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68d41afd0c39a807cfbd0cba_CCS%20Headshots%20(13)-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68d41afd0c39a807cfbd0cba_CCS%20Headshots%20(13)-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68d41afd0c39a807cfbd0cba_CCS%20Headshots%20(13)-p-1600.png 1600w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68d41afd0c39a807cfbd0cba_CCS%20Headshots%20(13).png 2000w" alt="" class="uui-testimonial15_customer-image"/></div><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-info"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-heading"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/adriannaalterman/">Michael Golub</a></div><div class="uui-text-size-small">CFO, Pano AI, Inc.<br/></div></div></div></div></div><div class="text-block-3"><strong class="bold-text-7">Table 3</strong></div><div class="text-block-2"><strong>Delivering climate benefits through land</strong><br/>Land is critical for energy deployment, biodiversity, carbon storage, food security, and more. As an asset class, it often outperforms equities while supporting sustainability. How can capital allocators and land managers find, optimize, and make better use of this limited resource? <br/></div><div class="text-block-3"></div><div class="w-row"><div class="w-col w-col-6"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-image-wrapper"><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc245b5789d87bbace240c_CCS%20Headshots%20(6).png" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 479px) 407px, (max-width: 767px) 198px, 180px" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc245b5789d87bbace240c_CCS%20Headshots%20(6)-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc245b5789d87bbace240c_CCS%20Headshots%20(6)-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc245b5789d87bbace240c_CCS%20Headshots%20(6)-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc245b5789d87bbace240c_CCS%20Headshots%20(6)-p-1600.png 1600w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc245b5789d87bbace240c_CCS%20Headshots%20(6).png 2000w" alt="" class="uui-testimonial15_customer-image"/></div><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-info"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-heading"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/dananmargason/">Danan Margason</a></div><div class="uui-text-size-small">Founder &amp; CEO, aarden.ai<br/></div></div></div></div><div class="w-col w-col-6"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-image-wrapper"><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc25ed950e0c31abbe78b3_CCS%20Headshots%20(7).png" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 479px) 407px, (max-width: 767px) 198px, 180px" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc25ed950e0c31abbe78b3_CCS%20Headshots%20(7)-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc25ed950e0c31abbe78b3_CCS%20Headshots%20(7)-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc25ed950e0c31abbe78b3_CCS%20Headshots%20(7)-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc25ed950e0c31abbe78b3_CCS%20Headshots%20(7)-p-1600.png 1600w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc25ed950e0c31abbe78b3_CCS%20Headshots%20(7).png 2000w" alt="" class="uui-testimonial15_customer-image"/></div><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-info"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-heading"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/adriannaalterman/">Isabella Todaro</a></div><div class="uui-text-size-small"> aarden.ai<br/></div></div></div></div></div><div class="text-block-3"><strong class="bold-text-7">Table 4</strong></div><div class="text-block-2"><strong>AI and Climate Capital</strong><br/>Trillions are earmarked for the energy transition, but deals can still take months or years to close–if at all. How can investors use AI to streamline origination, underwriting, and diligence, and accelerate their deployment into climate solutions?<br/></div><div class="text-block-3"></div><div class="w-row"><div class="w-col w-col-6"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-image-wrapper"><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc284a8c2ec2e8c2978c2e_CCS%20Headshots%20(8).png" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 479px) 407px, (max-width: 767px) 198px, 180px" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc284a8c2ec2e8c2978c2e_CCS%20Headshots%20(8)-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc284a8c2ec2e8c2978c2e_CCS%20Headshots%20(8)-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc284a8c2ec2e8c2978c2e_CCS%20Headshots%20(8)-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc284a8c2ec2e8c2978c2e_CCS%20Headshots%20(8)-p-1600.png 1600w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68cc284a8c2ec2e8c2978c2e_CCS%20Headshots%20(8).png 2000w" alt="" class="uui-testimonial15_customer-image"/></div><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-info"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-heading"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/mairi-robertson-b8716345/">Mairi Robertson</a></div><div class="uui-text-size-small">Director of Asset Financing, Ezra<br/></div></div></div></div><div class="w-col w-col-6"></div></div><div class="text-block-3"><strong class="bold-text-7">Table 5</strong></div><div class="text-block-2"><strong>The Future of Climate Exits: From M&amp;A to New Hybrids</strong><br/>Every climate company faces the same question: what does the endgame look like? Traditional exits such as M&amp;A remain the backbone, but new models like SPACs reimagined, asset holding companies, and creative carve outs are reshaping the path forward. This discussion will explore how founders, investors, and buyers can prepare for the deal structures that are defining climate’s next wave of growth.<br/></div><div class="text-block-3"></div><div class="w-row"><div class="w-col w-col-6"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-image-wrapper"><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/67f434084a10959b401aed6b_evan_bienstock_torso.webp" loading="lazy" alt="" class="uui-testimonial15_customer-image"/></div><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-info"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-heading">Evan Bienstock</div><div class="uui-text-size-small">Partner, Fenwick</div></div></div></div><div class="w-col w-col-6"></div></div><div class="text-block-3"><strong class="bold-text-7">Table 6</strong></div><div class="text-block-2"><strong>How do we talk about climate change with the American public in 2025?<br/></strong>The science is clear, the stakes are high, and yet the conversation too often stalls. Together, we’ll explore the art and science of climate communication today, surfacing strategies that help move the conversation from different perspectives toward shared solutions.<br/></div><div class="text-block-3"></div><div class="w-row"><div class="w-col w-col-11"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-image-wrapper"><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf4a01bcd863f214608a4_Tony%20(1).png" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 479px) 407px, (max-width: 767px) 198px, (max-width: 991px) 191px, 248px" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf4a01bcd863f214608a4_Tony%20(1)-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf4a01bcd863f214608a4_Tony%20(1)-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf4a01bcd863f214608a4_Tony%20(1)-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf4a01bcd863f214608a4_Tony%20(1)-p-1600.png 1600w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf4a01bcd863f214608a4_Tony%20(1).png 2000w" alt="" class="uui-testimonial15_customer-image"/></div><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-info"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-heading"><a href="https://environment.yale.edu/directory/faculty/anthony-leiserowitz" target="_blank"><strong>Anthony Leiserowitz</strong></a></div><div class="uui-text-size-small">JoshAni-TomKat Professor of Climate Communication at the Yale School of the Environment; Director of the Yale Program on Climate Change Communication<br/></div></div></div></div><div class="w-col w-col-1"></div></div><div class="text-block-3"><strong class="bold-text-7">Table 7</strong></div><div class="text-block-2"><strong>Nature as an Asset<br/></strong>Nature is not separate from the economy. This session explores the economic tools and policy frameworks emerging to bring natural capital into decision-making, and what it means to treat ecosystems not as externalities, but as essential infrastructure for the future.<br/></div><div class="text-block-3"></div><div class="w-row"><div class="w-col w-col-11"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-image-wrapper"><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf572e86e8c9895e55f76_Eli%20(1).png" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 479px) 407px, (max-width: 767px) 198px, (max-width: 991px) 191px, 248px" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf572e86e8c9895e55f76_Eli%20(1)-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf572e86e8c9895e55f76_Eli%20(1)-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf572e86e8c9895e55f76_Eli%20(1)-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf572e86e8c9895e55f76_Eli%20(1)-p-1600.png 1600w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf572e86e8c9895e55f76_Eli%20(1).png 2000w" alt="" class="uui-testimonial15_customer-image"/></div><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-info"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-heading"><a href="https://environment.yale.edu/directory/faculty/eli-fenichel" target="_blank"><strong>Eli Fenichel</strong></a></div><div class="uui-text-size-small">Knobloch Family Professor of Natural Resource Economics<br/></div></div></div></div><div class="w-col w-col-1"></div></div><div class="text-block-3"><strong class="bold-text-7">Table 8</strong></div><div class="text-block-2"><strong>Climate Change and Trade<br/></strong>The flows of goods, capital, and carbon are deeply intertwined. This session unpacks the tensions between open markets and environmental protection. Participants will leave with a sharper view of the risks and opportunities at the intersection of trade and law, in a warming world.<br/></div><div class="text-block-3"></div><div class="w-row"><div class="w-col w-col-11"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-image-wrapper"><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf59b2c4e69d53532c56b_Dan%20(1).png" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 479px) 407px, (max-width: 767px) 198px, (max-width: 991px) 191px, 248px" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf59b2c4e69d53532c56b_Dan%20(1)-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf59b2c4e69d53532c56b_Dan%20(1)-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf59b2c4e69d53532c56b_Dan%20(1)-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf59b2c4e69d53532c56b_Dan%20(1)-p-1600.png 1600w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf59b2c4e69d53532c56b_Dan%20(1).png 2000w" alt="" class="uui-testimonial15_customer-image"/></div><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-info"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-heading"><a href="https://environment.yale.edu/directory/faculty/daniel-c-esty" target="_blank"><strong>Daniel Esty</strong></a></div><div class="uui-text-size-small">Hillhouse Professor of Environmental Law and Policy, jointly with Yale Law School; Director of the Center for Environmental Law and Policy</div></div></div></div><div class="w-col w-col-1"></div></div><div class="text-block-3"><strong class="bold-text-7">Table 9</strong></div><div class="text-block-2"><strong>Do the Math on Climate Risk<br/></strong>Climate risk is no longer theoretical; it is showing up in balance sheets, supply chains, and boardrooms. Together, we’ll explore how to put numbers to uncertainty, transform abstract scenarios into actionable insight, and understand the role of risk as both a warning signal and a map for resilience.<br/></div><div class="text-block-3"></div><div class="w-row"><div class="w-col w-col-11"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-image-wrapper"><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf5d94f1402f28b4e1dc9_Todd%20Cort%20(1).png" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 479px) 407px, (max-width: 767px) 198px, (max-width: 991px) 191px, 248px" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf5d94f1402f28b4e1dc9_Todd%20Cort%20(1)-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf5d94f1402f28b4e1dc9_Todd%20Cort%20(1)-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf5d94f1402f28b4e1dc9_Todd%20Cort%20(1)-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf5d94f1402f28b4e1dc9_Todd%20Cort%20(1)-p-1600.png 1600w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/68bdf5d94f1402f28b4e1dc9_Todd%20Cort%20(1).png 2000w" alt="" class="uui-testimonial15_customer-image"/></div><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-info"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-heading"><a href="https://som.yale.edu/faculty-research/faculty-directory/todd-cort" target="_blank"><strong>Todd Cort</strong></a></div><div class="uui-text-size-small">Senior Lecturer in Sustainability; Faculty Director of Sustainability Program, MBA for Executives; Faculty Co-Director, Yale Center for Business and the Environment<br/></div></div></div></div><div class="w-col w-col-1"></div></div><div class="text-block-3"><strong class="bold-text-7">Table 10</strong></div><div class="text-block-2"><strong>How Climate Intelligence Improves Due Diligence and Protects Asset Value<br/>‍</strong>In a world of intensifying climate volatility, the real competitive edge lies in smarter investment decisions. This table will explore how forward-looking metrics, like return periods and site-specific hazard exposure, can: streamline due diligence, flag high-risk assets earlier, reduce consulting costs and turnaround time, justify adaptation and insurance strategies with data, align risk teams, asset managers, and boards around real exposure.<br/></div><div class="text-block-3"></div><div class="w-row"><div class="w-col w-col-11"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client"><div class="uui-testimonial15_client-image-wrapper"><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67cb7657527430c96178b797/